# inc-aocw: a monster that knows Minor Drain fires it at itself.
#
# The feyr (lib/mon3.irh:288) is the plainest carrier of the spell -- an
# ordinary monster, no template needed, and Minor Drain sits in its Spells
# list. A monster reaches either drain spell ONLY through the injury-remedy
# action (src/Monster.cpp:568-572), because the trouble code sits in the high
# word of Purpose and the plain attack slot's high word is zero. That action
# carries no target, and src/Magic.cpp reads "no victim and no coordinates" as
# "aim at me".
#
# THE SHAPE OF THIS FIXTURE, and why it is not simply "hit it and watch".
#
# Injury is only ONE of the feyr's troubles, and while it can see an enemy the
# attack action outranks the remedy. Hurting it in melee therefore proves
# nothing: it fights back, or flees, and never chooses the drain. What it
# needs is an injury and NO visible enemy. So:
#
#   1. Freeze Monsters, so the feyr cannot act while it is being set up.
#   2. Summon it five squares east, out of melee, so walking away later does
#      not open the Abort/Flee/Disengage prompt.
#   3. One cast of the player's own Minor Drain. One is enough: any damage at
#      all puts TROUBLE_INJURY in the list (src/Prayer.cpp:706). This cast is
#      also the CONTROL -- a spell the player aims must strike the feyr,
#      whatever the monster AI does with the same spell.
#   4. Walk ten squares west, out of its sight, while it is still frozen.
#   5. Thaw it and wait. Injured, with nobody to fight, it casts the drain.
#
# The feyr is off-screen by then, so the engine narrates none of it. The probe
# is the oracle, which is the whole reason the probe exists.
#
# Read by tools/check_drain_selfaim.sh on seed 4, with
# INCURSION_SELFAIM_PROBE=1 and INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat.

@include chargen-mage.keys

# chargen-mage.keys ends one keystroke earlier than chargen.keys does: the
# mage still has the arrival room description on screen. Dismiss it first, or
# the [w] below is eaten by the description and the verb menu opens instead.
ESC

# Wizard switches, counted from the top of the list in src/Tables.cpp:
#   3 Free Advancement, 4 Infinite Fatigue, 8 Infinite Mana,
#   11 Freeze Monsters.
#
# Know All Spells is deliberately NOT set. It fills the Spell Manager with
# every spell the class can reach, Minor Drain lands on a later page, and
# @choose reads only what is on the screen. Learn Any Spell below teaches the
# one spell this fixture needs and leaves the list one page long.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*2
SPACE
DOWN
SPACE
DOWN*4
SPACE
DOWN*3
SPACE
@dump:switches
ESC

# One level, so the mage survives the walk and the wait.
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Minor Drain" ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Aberration"
@choose "feyr"
RIGHT*5
ENTER
@dump:feyr-summoned

# The control cast. [RIGHT] both aims and fires; no ENTER follows it.
m
@choose "Minor Drain"
RIGHT
@dump:feyr-hurt
@expect "Your necromantic bolt strikes a feyr."

LEFT*10
@dump:walked-away

# Thaw: switch 11 again.
w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

s*30
@dump:after-thaw
v
@dump:messages
ESC
@quit
